<title>USA: CP&amp;L Robinson nuke seen on line Saturday.</title>
<headline>CP&amp;L Robinson nuke seen on line Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power &amp; Light Co's 683 megawatt Robinson nuclear power unit 2 was expected to resume output this weekend following an outage for scheduled refueling and maintenance, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect to synchronize to the grid on Saturday night,&quot; spokeswoman Ann Mary Carley said Thursday.</p>
<p>The Harsville, S.C. unit was taken off line Sept 7 for an expected 50-days of maintenance and refueling.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
